+# --- header / section 12 checkpoint binding -----------------------------------------------------
+
+static func checkpoint_binding_refusal(header: Header, section12_next_high: int,
+		section12_next_low: int, section1_completed_tick: int) -> Refusal:
+	"""Refuse unless the header's redundant checkpoint equals section 12's pair and section 1's tick.
+
+	SAVE-REPLAY-R01 version 2's deliberately narrow binding validator. It takes an already
+	decoded Header and three plain integers the caller read from that same decoded file, and it
+	owns only the association of those scalars. It preloads no section, scheduler, commands or
+	world-runtime module, reads no disk, touches no store or clock, restores nothing, admits
+	nothing and reserves no sequence. The header is a redundant declaration; section 12 remains
+	the allocator owner.
+
+	Precedence: a null Header is REFUSE_VALUE_RANGE; an invalid outer version, header size or
+	table offset is the existing version gate's refusal; nonzero reserved padding is
+	REFUSE_RESERVED_NONZERO; either malformed allocator pair is REFUSE_SEQUENCE_RANGE; either
+	negative tick is REFUSE_NEGATIVE_TICK; and only then does a well-formed but unequal high,
+	low or tick give REFUSE_CHECKPOINT_MISMATCH. Only exact equality accepts.
+
+	This is not a whole-header, body or world validator. The full coordinator separately
+	validates file extents, identities, every section's own semantics, the clock maximum,
+	pending references and the canonical state digest before any live-array write.
+	"""
+	if header == null:
+		return Refusal.new(REFUSE_VALUE_RANGE, "no header was supplied to bind against")
+	var version: Refusal = _version_refusal(header)
+	if not version.is_ok():
+		return version
+	var checkpoint: Refusal = checkpoint_refusal(header)
+	if not checkpoint.is_ok():
+		return checkpoint
+	if not is_sequence_pair_valid(section12_next_high, section12_next_low):
+		return Refusal.new(REFUSE_SEQUENCE_RANGE,
+			"the section 12 pair (high %d, low %d) is neither an ordinary u32 pair nor (%d, %d)"
+				% [section12_next_high, section12_next_low, SEQUENCE_TERMINAL_HIGH,
+					SEQUENCE_TERMINAL_LOW])
+	if header.completed_tick < 0 or section1_completed_tick < 0:
+		return Refusal.new(REFUSE_NEGATIVE_TICK,
+			"header tick %d and section 1 tick %d must both be nonnegative"
+				% [header.completed_tick, section1_completed_tick])
